native:
Among the sons of earth, a thing apart;
For I was born, far from my native clime,
Under the white man’s menace, out of time.

nation:
The distant nations heard the word,
Build me a nation true and strong,
Bar out the old world's hate and wrong;

nature:
Co'se, I knows dat Suke 's contra'y, an' she moughty ap' to vex;
But you got to mek erlowance fu' de nature of huh sex;
Dat ol' mare o' mine.

nature's:
And most prosaic patience. You, you are young
As Eve with nature’s daybreak on her face;
But this same world you are come to, dearest coz,
